[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cannot deliver a signal to the child at the right instant. It was found by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reading the reader against glibc's behaviour, and `stdin_delivered_in_slow_chunks`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m covers the neighbouring case (a short read must not look like EOF).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Behaviours checked and confirmed already correct
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m No stdout, stderr or exit-status difference was observed on any other input.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7500 randomised inputs (random bytes, scanf-alphabet soup, operands jittered
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m around every 32- and 64-bit boundary, long digit runs, whitespace soup)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m produced zero mismatches, as did the enumerated suite. Specifically confirmed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`scanf` return value is discarded.** A conversion that never happens leaves
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   its variable at `1`. Empty input, whitespace-only input and `xyz` all print
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `quotient: 1, remainder: 0`; `42` alone divides by the default `y == 1`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`%d` reads across newlines.** `\n\n\n5\n\n\n2` is `5 / 2`, not a failed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   read. Whitespace skipping covers exactly the C-locale `isspace` set
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`' '`, `\t`, `\n`, `\v`, `\f`, `\r`); `0x85` and `0xa0` are not whitespace,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and `LC_ALL` cannot change that because the program never calls `setlocale`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Ordering of the two conversions.** `scanf` stops at the first failure, so a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   bad `x` means `y` is never even attempted. `abc 10 3` prints
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `quotient: 1, remainder: 0` — the `10` is not consumed into `y`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **One byte of lookahead is pushed back.** `10 3abc`, `5,2`, `0x10 2`, `3.9 2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and `5e2 3` all stop the conversion at the offending byte.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **strtol saturation, then truncation into `int`.** Out-of-range literals clamp
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   to `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` and are then truncated: `4294967297` → `1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `4294967295` → `-1`, `9223372036854775807` → `-1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `-9223372036854775808` → `0`, and a 1000-digit run of `9`s → `-1`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`0` when negated). Leading zeros and a `+` sign do not change any of this.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`div` truncates toward zero,** so the remainder takes the sign of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   dividend: `-7 / 2` is `-3` remainder `-1`, and `7 / -2` is `-3` remainder `1`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Verified over the full grid of operands in `-6..=6`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Undefined division traps rather than returning.** `div(x, 0)` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `div(INT_MIN, -1)` reach `idiv` with no representable result, so the process
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   dies of `SIGFPE` (no exit code, empty stdout, empty stderr). This includes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   divisors that only become zero after truncation, e.g. `4294967296` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `18446744073709551616`. The Rust side reproduces it by executing the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `idiv` instruction; a checked or wrapping division would exit `0` instead and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   is caught by `division_by_zero_traps` and `int_min_over_minus_one_traps`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`printf` formatting**, including the `", "` separator and exactly one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   trailing newline.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`argv` is ignored** (`main` takes no parameters), and stdin from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `/dev/null`, from a closed descriptor, and delivered in 20 ms chunks all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   behave identically.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
